<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Buss, Anderson & Perry (2015) Biol. Bull., Dudgeon et al. (1999) Am. Nat. & Blackstone (1999) Syst. Biol. colonial hydroid pulsatile gastrovascular stolon network, anastomosis loop closure, and runner-to-sheet morphospace — MorphoEval overall 51.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2020-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net.py` (weighted score: 53.0/100). The Pass 1 baseline integrates only a single-stolon lumen radius ODE at two pump gain values without solving the multi-node Kirchhoff gastrovascular pressure network driven by active polyp contraction oscillators V_p(t) = V_0 + Delta_V sin(omega_p t + phi_p), omits spatial stolon tip outgrowth, tip-to-stolon anastomosis loop closure (b_1 = E - V + 1), and low-shear stolon regression across the Blackstone (1999) / Buss (2015) runner-to-sheet continuum (Podocoryna runner, 2,4-DNP uncoupled shift, Hydractinia web, Hydractinia dense sheet, and polyp-excision / MgCl2 paralysis control), and does not segment the vendored Hydractinia symbiolongicarpus colony micrograph. Overall 51.9/100 (faithfulness 49.1, reproducibility 58.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 54, Morphological realism / specimen match 44, Parameter expressivity 49, Morphometric validation 51, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 55, Reproducibility package 53. Output judged: docs/media/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net.py at 8871db0, image/png, 100328 B, 1200×504 px, artifact_sha256 08ee845e9749730b66c536156a27ccec1a38f396729cccb6dbc8bd94db099a6a (sha256 08ee845e9749730b66c536156a27ccec1a38f396729cccb6dbc8bd94db099a6a), spec_fingerprint 89c0f33a7d88261f666404a05447dcbcee682836ef33db2cdc94324f94c96aa2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 89c0f33a7d88261f666404a05447dcbcee682836ef33db2cdc94324f94c96aa2; artifact_sha256: 08ee845e9749730b66c536156a27ccec1a38f396729cccb6dbc8bd94db099a6a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net_reference.json=db4c51ae3bdeb00a..., datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/hydractinia_symbiolongicarpus_specimen.jpg=059b83cd797d0516..., datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/paper_citations.bib=44b19ab180b9e27a..., datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/scout_manifest.json=626e17690a5a1cd7...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement the coupled pulsatile polyp oscillator + multi-node Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff gastrovascular pressure solver sum_j G_ij*(p_i(t) - p_j(t)) = -dV_p/dt with quartic lumen conductance G_ij = pi*r_ij^4/(8*mu*L_ij) and wall shear stress tau_w = 4*mu*|Q_ij|/(pi*r_ij^3).",
        "remediation needed: Segment the vendored Yale Peabody Museum Hydractinia symbiolongicarpus colony micrograph (`hydractinia_symbiolongicarpus_specimen.jpg`, YPM IZ 080458) to extract coenosarc mat area coverage, endodermal gastrovascular polyp pump centers, planar meshedness alpha, and Euler cyclomatic loops b_1, backed by runtime SHA-256 verification and an 8-suite `--self-test`.",
        "remediation needed: Simulate spatial stolon tip outgrowth, tip-to-stolon anastomosis loop closure (b_1 = E - V + 1), and low-shear stolon regression across the 5 canonical Blackstone (1999) / Buss (2015) morphospace regimes (Podocoryna runner, 2,4-DNP redox uncoupling shift, Hydractinia intermediate web, Hydractinia dense stolonal sheet, and polyp-excision / MgCl2 contraction arrest control) plus an 8-point pump-amplitude sweep." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.19e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

